        "urls": [
          {
            "display_url": "cdn.deepseek.com/policies/en-US…",
            "end": 795,
            "expanded_url": "https://cdn.deepseek.com/policies/en-US/deepseek-privacy-policy.html",
            "start": 772,
            "url": "https://t.co/BMM9ALAAcm"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "I carefully reviewed their documentation and found that indeed there is no clear retention period for this data.\n\n> How Long Do We Keep Your Personal Data\n> We retain Personal Data for as long as necessary to provide our Services and for the other purposes set out in this Privacy Policy. We also retain Personal Data when necessary to comply with contractual and legal obligations, when we have a legitimate business interest to do so (such as improving and developing our Services and enhancing their safety, security and stability), and for the exercise or defense of legal claims.\n> The retention periods will be different depending on the amount, type and sensitivity of Personal Data, the purposes for which we use the Personal Data and any legal requirements, etc.\nhttps://t.co/BMM9ALAAcm\n\nIt mentions a \"necessary\" period, but it doesn't specify a concrete retention timeline. This is indeed something Chinese companies often don't pay much attention to.\n\nMaybe you could try a third-party provider? After all, it's an open-source model."
    },
